BEHAVIOR copy-file

DESCRIPTION
  Copies source file to destination using the stdlib io convenience behaviors
  (read-file-all + write-file-all) instead of a hand-rolled open/read/write/
  close loop. bytes_copied = bytes written (>= 0 on success; write-file-all
  returns a negative count if the destination cannot be written). A missing
  source reads as empty (the runtime guards a bad fd), so it copies 0 bytes.

CONTRACT
  INPUT source_path string
  INPUT dest_path string
  OUTPUT bytes_copied int 8

  REQUIRES read-file-all@bf59f1e1 write-file-all@b17d9aa8

  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH fabb7c66

COMPOSITION
  rd = CALL read-file-all source_path
  wr = CALL write-file-all dest_path rd.data rd.length
  SET bytes_copied wr.bytes_written
END
